      "message": "nit; It might be worth updating this comment to let readers know why this is ok and needed. \n\nI.e., something like:\n\nThe system server is allowed to go over the request count limit when it is creating requests on behalf of another app (but not itself). This is ok since it only happens in the per-app API flows in which case, after the new requests are created as part of a reassignment, the old requests for that particular app UID will be removed resulting in a net increase of requests of \u00270\u0027. This is unfortunately necessary since with the current architecture since the old requests can\u0027t be removed until after the new requests are created.",
